# MP3 ID3v2 Tag Reader and Editor (C Language)

## Project Overview

This project is a command-line based MP3 ID3v2 Tag Reader and Editor implemented using the C programming language.
It allows the user to view and edit MP3 metadata such as Title, Artist, Album, Year, Genre, and Comment
without affecting the original audio frames.

The project follows the ID3v2 standard and edits metadata by rebuilding ID3 frames using a temporary file,
which is a safe technique used by real MP3 tag editors.

## Features

### View MP3 Metadata
- Title
- Artist
- Album
- Year
- Genre
- Comment

### Edit MP3 Metadata
- Edit any supported tag
- Allows metadata values of different lengths
- Uses temporary file replacement to prevent file corruption
- Preserves original audio data

## Concepts Used
- File handling in C (`fopen`, `fread`, `fwrite`, `fseek`)
- MP3 ID3v2 tag structure
- Big-endian byte order handling
- Bitwise operations
- Frame-based metadata replacement
- Temporary file replacement technique

## Project Files Structure

├── main.c   → Handles user input (view / edit / help)  
├── view.c   → Displays MP3 metadata  
├── edit.c   → Edits MP3 metadata  
├── view.h   → Header file for view function  
├── edit.h   → Header file for edit and help functions  
├── sample.mp3 → Input MP3 file  
└── README.md → Project documentation  

## How to Compile

```bash
gcc *.c
./a.out
 ```  